{"id":"painters","title":"Painters with the most expensive paintings sold","prompt":"Name the 10 painters whose priciest painting sold for the most (the price paid, not adjusted for inflation)","noun":"painters","category":"Culture","metric":"Their priciest painting sold (price paid)","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of most expensive paintings","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_expensive_paintings","asOf":"2026-11-18","dataAsOf":"2026"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Leonardo da Vinci","aliases":["Leonardo de Vinci","Leonardo DaVinci","Da Vinci","Davinci","Leonardo Davinchi","Leonardo di ser Piero da Vinci","Leonard da Vinci","Leonardo da Vinchi","The Great Leonardo","Léonard de Vinci","L. Da Vinci","Leanardo da vinci","Leonardo Di Vinci","Leo da vinci","Da Vincian","Leonardo Abince","De vinci","Leonardo","Di Vinci","Vinci"],"value":"$450.3 million","n":450.3,"article":"Leonardo da Vinci","fact":{"text":"Salvator Mundi sold for $450.3 million in 2017. In 1958 it had gone for £45, as a work by one of his pupils.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvator_Mundi_(Leonardo)"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Willem de Kooning","aliases":["Willem DeKooning","William de Kooning","William dekooning","DeKooning","William de Koonig","de Kooning","Kooning"],"value":"$300 million","n":300,"article":"Willem de Kooning","fact":{"text":"Interchange went to Ken Griffin for $300 million in 2015. De Kooning had sold it in 1955 for $4,000.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interchange_(de_Kooning)"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Paul Cézanne","aliases":["Cézanne","Paul cezane","Cézannesque","Cézannian"],"value":"$250 million","n":250,"article":"Paul Cézanne","fact":{"text":"One of his five Card Players went to Qatar's royal family in 2011 for an estimated $250 million, a record until 2017.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Card_Players"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Gustav Klimt","aliases":["Klimt","Gustave Klimt","Gustav Kilmt","Gustav Klimmt","Gustav Klimpt","Gustov Klimt","Gustaf Klimt","Klimtian"],"value":"$236.4 million","n":236.4,"article":"Gustav Klimt","fact":{"text":"Portrait of Elisabeth Lederer sold for $236.4 million in 2025. To escape the Nazis, she claimed Klimt was her father.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portrait_of_Elisabeth_Lederer"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Paul Gauguin","aliases":["Gauguin","Eugene Henri Paul Gauguin","Paul Gaugin","Gaugin","Gaugan","Gogan"],"value":"$210 million","n":210,"article":"Paul Gauguin","fact":{"text":"When Will You Marry?, painted in Tahiti in 1892, was sold privately to Qatar in 2015 for close to $210 million.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/When_Will_You_Marry%3F"}},{"rank":6,"name":"Jackson Pollock","aliases":["Jackson Pollack","Paul Jackson Pollock","Jackson Polluck","Pollockian","Pollock"],"value":"$200 million","n":200,"article":"Jackson Pollock","fact":{"text":"Ken Griffin paid $200 million for the drip painting Number 17A in 2015. It was in the 1949 Life story that made Pollock famous.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Number_17A"}},{"rank":7,"name":"Rembrandt","aliases":["Rembrandt van Rijn","Rembrandt Harmenzsoon van Rijn","Rembrandt Harmensz van Rijn","Rembrant","Van Rejn","Rembrandt Harmenszoon van Rijn","Remberandt","Rembrant van Rijn","Reimbrond Vainrein","Rembrand van Rijn","Rembrand","Rembrandt van Riji","Rembrandt Harmenszoon van Ryn","Rembrandt van Ryn"],"value":"$198 million","n":198,"article":"Rembrandt","fact":{"text":"The Netherlands bought his self-portrait The Standard Bearer from the Rothschilds for €175 million in 2022.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Standard_Bearer_(Rembrandt,_1636)"}},{"rank":8,"name":"Andy Warhol","aliases":["Warhol","Andy worhol","Andrew warhola","Andy Warhaul","Andrew Warhol","Andy Warhola","Drella","Andy Wahrol","Warholian Pop","Warholesque","Warholian","Warholite","Andrew Warhola Jr."],"value":"$195 million","n":195,"article":"Andy Warhol","fact":{"text":"Shot Sage Blue Marilyn sold for $195 mi